{
  "priority": "continuous-queue",
  "rationale": "The fabric is bottlenecked by manual human initiation for every batch, preventing autonomous procurement. While semantic quality and schema mapping are tactical, the inability to operate as a persistent, unattended service prevents the transition from a CLI-based test tool to a functional, scalable infrastructure for colonies.",
  "firstPatch": "Implement a lightweight daemon layer (e.g., using a file watcher or an SQS-like queue consumer) that continuously monitors a watch-directory or message broker for incoming job JSONL files, auto-invoking the dispatcher logic instead of requiring CLI-based trigger commands.",
  "risk": "Introducing a persistent background process increases the risk of 'zombie' jobs if the error-handling circuit breaker fails or if the registry-priced cost estimation logic does not account for infinite-loop retries in an autonomous environment."
}

